**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests`

**How to implement.** The EF Core wiring proof goes with its only consumer and its MSSQL settings; the library model replaces it in the next step (001 §R 'The `Test` EF table and its initial migration'; 001 §C 'No migrations'; .spec-md §3.18 'One local database', §7 '`Test` EF table + migration → library model'). This step only deletes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Database/`: delete `Test.cs`, `TestDbContext.cs` and the `Migrations/` folder with its three files (`20260711000000_Initial.cs`, `20260711000000_Initial.Designer.cs`, `TestDbContextModelSnapshot.cs`). In `OpticalConstructor.Database.csproj`, delete the Spec 0038 Part M comment block above the first `PropertyGroup`: it says the project only proves EF wiring and that no product project references it, and both stop being true here and in the next step. Its properties, its NU1903 comment and its `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` reference stay, so the project compiles with no source for this one step. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/`: delete `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` and `fixtures/database-appsettings.json`. In `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, delete the `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` compile item with its comment, the `fixtures\database-appsettings.json` Content item with its comment, the `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` PackageReference with its comment, and the `OpticalConstructor.App` and `OpticalConstructor.Database` ProjectReferences with their shared comment. `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` is the only test file that opens `OpticalConstructor.App`, `OpticalConstructor.Database` or EF Core, and the next step's tests reach the model and EF Core through Storage's reference. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`, module `ConfigKey`: delete `databaseProvider` (`:44-48`) and `mssqlConnectionString` (`:50-53`) with their docs, because their only reader was `TestDbMigrationTests` (.spec-md §3.18; 001 §W excludes cloud or shared databases). `sqliteConnectionString` (`:55-58`) stays; its doc becomes one line saying it is the library database's SQLite connection string, read through `AppSettingsProvider.tryGetConnectionString` (001 §C 'Settings'; spec 0050). The module doc (`:14-20`) drops '— and the Part M storage proof (step 40) —'. No other key, default or comment changes, and `OpticalConstructor.App/appsettings.json` is untouched, because it holds no database key. Nothing replaces the deleted facts: `TestDbMigrationTests`' seven cases (the four `DatabaseProvider.tryCreate` rows, the unknown-provider fact, the provider-choice fact and the migration fact) lower the constructor suite's count on purpose.

**Acceptance.** After the retirement, `Test.cs`, `TestDbContext.cs`, the `Migrations/` folder, `TestDbMigrationTests.fs` and `fixtures/database-appsettings.json` MUST NOT exist; `git grep -n -i -E "TestDbContext|TestDbMigrationTests|database-appsettings|DatabaseProvider|mssql|EFC-wiring" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with exactly `TestDbMigrationTests`' seven cases fewer; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.
